Switch: depth EFB copies on the deko3d NRO (AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D; issue #9, the depth of field)

The deko3d NRO leaves CoreFeaturesAndLimits off (as the GL NRO's adapter did), and tex_copy_conv only made
its depth conversions with it: needs_conversion(GX_TF_Z16) was false, so GXCopyTex gave the depth of
field's Z16 copy an RGBA8 colour texture and switch/deko/aurora blitted the depth view into it as colour.
The composite read no depth and the effect never showed. With AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D the depth formats are
registered without the core features (the deko3d encoder converts them with its own fixed shaders).

--- a/lib/gfx/tex_copy_conv.cpp	2026-10-17 16:19:30
+++ b/lib/gfx/tex_copy_conv.cpp	2026-10-17 16:19:30
@@ -526,6 +526,17 @@
     }
   }
   // Skip depth copies in compatibility mode
+#if defined(AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D)
+  // the deko3d NRO: switch/deko/aurora/dk_encode.cpp converts depth copies with its own shaders (tex_copy_conv_z8,
+  // _z16); registering these formats makes GXCopyTex give them a conversion texture instead of an RGBA8 colour copy
+  // (the depth of field's Z16 copy). g_hasCoreFeatures stays off: the GX pipeline configs, and so the pipeline
+  // cache, are unchanged.
+  if (!webgpu::g_hasCoreFeatures) {
+    for (const auto& conv : DepthConvPipelines) {
+      g_pipelines[conv.fmt] = create_pipeline(conv, DepthShaderPreamble, g_depthBindGroupLayout);
+    }
+  }
+#endif
   if (webgpu::g_hasCoreFeatures) {
     for (const auto& conv : DepthConvPipelines) {
       g_pipelines[conv.fmt] = create_pipeline(conv, DepthShaderPreamble, g_depthBindGroupLayout);
